    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0890" n="1724" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1575</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-17T13:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 17, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1565. Embassy’s 1776, September 5, 1 p.m. Department is inclined to doubt the
                    wisdom of your intimating to Spanish Government that War Trade Board may
                    discontinue its practice in excepting Spanish vessels from bunker negotiations.
                    In view of the satisfactory financial agreement which has just been concluded,
                    it is felt that such an intimation of intention to exert further pressure might
                    not be well <pb facs="0891" n="1725" xml:id="pg1725"/> received even though the
                    intimation is only made for the purpose of later withdrawing it. Your further
                    views are desired.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
